	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:04,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 4160
			},
			"text": " This question comes from Noah, who asks what if the Earth were made entirely of protons"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:04,160",
				"to": "00:00:06,660"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 4160,
				"to": 6660
			},
			"text": " and the Moon were made entirely of electrons?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:06,660",
				"to": "00:00:12,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 6660,
				"to": 12120
			},
			"text": " This is, by far, the most destructive what-if scenario to date."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:12,120",
				"to": "00:00:15,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 12120,
				"to": 15560
			},
			"text": " You might imagine an electron Moon orbiting a proton Earth, sort of like a gigantic hydrogen"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:15,560",
				"to": "00:00:16,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 15560,
				"to": 16560
			},
			"text": " atom."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:16,560",
				"to": "00:00:17,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 16560,
				"to": 17900
			},
			"text": " On one level, it sort of makes sense."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:17,900",
				"to": "00:00:20,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 17900,
				"to": 20200
			},
			"text": " Electrons orbit protons and Moons orbit planets."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:20,200",
				"to": "00:00:23,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 20200,
				"to": 23720
			},
			"text": " However, electron Moons do not orbit proton planets."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:23,720",
				"to": "00:00:26,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 23720,
				"to": 26780
			},
			"text": " If you put two negatively charged electrons together, they try to fly apart with a force"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:26,780",
				"to": "00:00:30,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 26780,
				"to": 30400
			},
			"text": " about 20 orders of magnitude stronger than the gravity pulling them together."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:30,400",
				"to": "00:00:34,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 30400,
				"to": 34160
			},
			"text": " If you put 10^53 electrons together to build a Moon, they push each other apart with an"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:34,160",
				"to": "00:00:35,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 34160,
				"to": 35960
			},
			"text": " unbelievable amount of energy."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,960",
				"to": "00:00:39,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35960,
				"to": 39160
			},
			"text": " The Moon and Earth would have no chance to gravitationally or even electrostatically"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:39,160",
				"to": "00:00:43,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 39160,
				"to": 43120
			},
			"text": " influence each other, the forces trying to blow each one apart would be far more powerful."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:43,120",
				"to": "00:00:45,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 43120,
				"to": 45840
			},
			"text": " If we ignore general relativity for a minute, we'll come back to it."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:45,840",
				"to": "00:00:48,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 45840,
				"to": 48520
			},
			"text": " We can calculate that the energy from all these electrons all pushing on each other"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:48,520",
				"to": "00:00:51,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 48520,
				"to": 51640
			},
			"text": " would be enough to accelerate all of them outward at nearly the speed of light."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:51,640",
				"to": "00:00:55,280"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 51640,
				"to": 55280
			},
			"text": " But this is one of those situations where saying \"nearly the speed of light\" isn't very meaningful."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:55,280",
				"to": "00:00:59,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 55280,
				"to": 59320
			},
			"text": " The electrons in a normal particle accelerator also go nearly the speed of light, but the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:59,320",
				"to": "00:01:02,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 59320,
				"to": 62680
			},
			"text": " electrons in the exploding Moon each have orders of magnitude more than the Planck energy,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:02,680",
				"to": "00:01:06,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 62680,
				"to": 66400
			},
			"text": " which is itself many orders of magnitude larger than the energies we can reach in our largest"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:06,400",
				"to": "00:01:07,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 66400,
				"to": 67400
			},
			"text": " accelerators."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:07,400",
				"to": "00:01:09,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 67400,
				"to": 69840
			},
			"text": " In other words, Noah's question takes us pretty far outside normal physics into the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:09,840",
				"to": "00:01:13,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 69840,
				"to": 73140
			},
			"text": " highly theoretical realm of things like quantum gravity and string theory."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,140",
				"to": "00:01:15,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73140,
				"to": 75800
			},
			"text": " So I contacted a string theorist, and I explained Noah's scenario."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:15,800",
				"to": "00:01:19,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 75800,
				"to": 79120
			},
			"text": " Dr. Keeler agreed that we shouldn't rely on calculations to give that much energy to"
